  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The v7 table, as measured",
      "items": [
        "qwen7b 72.0 · gemma2:2b 71.0 · llama3.2:3b 70.5 · qwen2.5:3b 65.5",
        "The 7B did not move while every small model gained 5–9: a 10.5-point gap became 1.0, inside the band"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What makes two numbers comparable",
      "items": [
        "A round file names its own test set — read that field before comparing anything",
        "A prompt or label change makes every crib stale, and a round refuses a stale crib",
        "gemini is the hosted baseline: host-side only, and --rag is refused — the crib is the answer key",
        "The crib is example_embedding (pgvector, k=5, leave-one-out); a label change makes it stale and a round refuses it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Two automated readers, one human ruling",
      "items": [
        "The reviewer is a separate model session with a clean context; it checks the claim against the code",
        "The evaluator gates whether the number means what it says — also a model session",
        "The owner rules the model. That is the one human decision in this loop, and it is not delegated"
      ]
    }
  ]
}